From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:23:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/common/spi: Decode 4-bit FLCOMP densities from the 8
 series on

The size of the boot flash is read from the descriptor's FLCOMP, with
3-bit density fields for each component. From the 8 series (Lynx Point)
on, the fields are 4 bits wide, bits 3:0 and 7:4, which is also how a
descriptor says 32 or 64 MiB. A ThinkPad W541 with FLCOMP 0x34, an
8 MiB and a 4 MiB chip, came out as 8 + 32 MiB: "SF size 0x2800000
does not correspond to CONFIG_ROM_SIZE 0xc00000!!" at every boot, and
a bounds check on writes 28 MiB too loose.

Use 4-bit fields on Lynx Point and Wildcat Point.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541: the message is gone, flash size 0xc00000.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/common/spi.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/common/spi.c b/src/southbridge/intel/common/spi.c
index b340dcbeb..59bc4ec56 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/common/spi.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/common/spi.c
@@ -956,12 +956,23 @@ static int spi_flash_programmer_probe(const struct spi_slave *spi,
 		break;
 	}
 
-	flash->size = 1 << (19 + (cntlr.flcomp & 7));
+	/*
+	 * FLCOMP: the density of each component, 3-bit fields (bits 2:0 and
+	 * 5:3) up to the 7 series, 4-bit fields (bits 3:0 and 7:4) from the
+	 * 8 series (Lynx Point) on, which also lets a descriptor encode 32
+	 * and 64 MiB components.
+	 */
+	const bool flcomp_wide = CONFIG(SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_LYNXPOINT) ||
+				 CONFIG(SOUTHBRIDGE_INTEL_WILDCATPOINT);
+	const unsigned int density_bits = flcomp_wide ? 4 : 3;
+	const unsigned int density_mask = (1 << density_bits) - 1;
+
+	flash->size = 1 << (19 + (cntlr.flcomp & density_mask));
 
 	flash->ops = &spi_flash_ops;
 
 	if ((cntlr.hsfs & HSFS_FDV) && ((cntlr.flmap0 >> 8) & 3))
-		flash->size += 1 << (19 + ((cntlr.flcomp >> 3) & 7));
+		flash->size += 1 << (19 + ((cntlr.flcomp >> density_bits) & density_mask));
 	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "flash size 0x%x bytes\n", flash->size);
 
 	return 0;
